      "writtenOn": "2026-10-22T21:36:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nathan: Thank you very much for the patch. After taking a look at the patch, I decided to decline it.\n\nIn general the [kinds of patches covered by the Patch Rewards Program](https://bughunters.google.com/about/rules/open-source/patch-rewards-program-rules#qualifying-submissions) are good coding practices. For example, this patch falls under the category \"Refactorings that make it easier to reason about the security properties of the code\". However, for a mature and stable code base such as the VP8 and VP9 **decoders** in libvpx, it may make sense to follow the principle of \"if it ain\u0027t broke, don\u0027t fix it\" for two reasons:\n- It takes time for us to review this patch.\n- This patch changes the pattern of calling `decrypt_cb`. For example, in the `vp9_parse_superframe_index()` function, a single `decrypt_cb` call of `frames * mag` bytes is replaced by `frames` `decrypt_cb` calls of `mag` bytes each. This is a potential source of bug if a particular `decrypt_cb` implementation depends on the current calling pattern.",
      "parentUuid": "cdab18eb_5994ce70",
      "revId": "c1134e9f9e6a1e094307e0f4d09e11e16cc6dff8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
  ],
